 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by the idempotency key lookup not filtering by user_id, allowing cross-user key reuse. The fix adds a user_id filter to the database query in tracker/idempotency.py, ensuring that idempotency keys are scoped to each user.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/idempotency.py b/tracker/idempotency.py\nindex d7208d6..f25cdf7 100644\n--- a/tracker/idempotency.py\n+++ b/tracker/idempotency.py\n@@ -20,10 +20,7 @@ class IdempotencyStore:\n         Re-using a key with a different payload is a client error (409).\n         \"\"\"\n         with self.db.connection() as conn:\n-            row = conn.execute(\n-                \"SELECT fingerprint, status, body FROM idempotency_keys WHERE key = ?\",\n-                (key,),\n-            ).fetchone()\n+            row = conn.execute(\"SELECT fingerprint, status, body FROM idempotency_keys WHERE key = ? AND user_id = ?\", (key, user_id),).fetchone()\n         if row is None:\n             return None\n         if row[\"fingerprint\"] != fingerprint(payload):\n",
